1
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:54,971
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

2
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:57,057
Wait…

3
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,933
EPISODE 5

4
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:01,352
Unbelievable.

5
00:01:01,936 --> 00:01:03,730
I went out of my way to call him.

6
00:01:05,023 --> 00:01:06,900
I spoke to him in English

7
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:09,861
so the operator wouldn't understand,
but he didn't even thank me.

8
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:17,744
My goodness.

9
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:19,079
You scared me.

10
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:20,914
Why are you standing here?

11
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,291
Are you going home?

12
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,919
Sorry? You told me to leave for the day.

13
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:29,172
I forgot I was supposed to treat you well.

14
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:32,467
- Let's go to the photo studio.
- The photo studio?

15
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,719
I'm going with you to the photo studio.

16
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:39,224
Well, I suppose a photo studio picture
is better than a newspaper one.

17
00:01:40,058 --> 00:01:41,226
Let's go. Come with me.

18
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:03,975
Where are they shooting from?

19
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,143
Where did it come from?

20
00:04:15,046 --> 00:04:16,005
Are you all right?

21
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:22,971
Get in!

22
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:26,557
Let's go.

23
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:31,521
Damn it. Get in!

24
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:41,781
Get in!

25
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:58,298
Jeong-yeop, stay awake.

26
00:04:58,381 --> 00:05:00,049
You have to stay awake.

27
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,093
Wake up, you punk!

28
00:05:03,219 --> 00:05:05,388
Jeong-yeop!

29
00:05:13,813 --> 00:05:14,647
Chief!

30
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:35,001
Over there!

31
00:06:04,405 --> 00:06:05,281
Break it!

32
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:13,206
Second floor, go!

33
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:24,008
He went that way.

34
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,430
He ran out that way.

35
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:33,017
It's a tall, young guy with a mask on.

36
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:53,746
There's no one here.

37
00:06:58,543 --> 00:06:59,710
- That way.
- Yes, sir!

38
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:43,963
What do we have here?

39
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:46,924
Close the curtains!

40
00:07:47,508 --> 00:07:49,886
She's the daughter of the president
of Joil Textile Factory.

41
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:05,943
Joil Textile Factory.

42
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:08,446
She came to get custom clothes fitted.

43
00:08:08,529 --> 00:08:11,407
We heard a commotion outside
and locked the door.

44
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:14,327
The culprit was hiding upstairs.

45
00:08:15,411 --> 00:08:17,371
How am I supposed to believe that?

46
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:22,919
Here's my card.

47
00:08:24,295 --> 00:08:25,713
JOIL

48
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:30,885
The president will be having dinner
with the governor-general next week.

49
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:32,887
That said,

50
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:36,182
if he hears that the police pulled open
the changing room curtain

51
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:39,727
on his precious only daughter,

52
00:08:40,561 --> 00:08:43,689
I don't think he would be too happy.

53
00:08:57,119 --> 00:08:58,162
Sorry about that.

54
00:09:13,052 --> 00:09:14,262
Young-bok!

55
00:09:15,388 --> 00:09:16,222
Young-bok.

56
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:20,017
Young-bok, stay with me.

57
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:22,895
Young-bok.

58
00:09:30,861 --> 00:09:31,862
Miss.

59
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,073
Are you all right?

60
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:38,828
Oh no, Young-bok.

61
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:41,581
Young-bok.

62
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:45,001
Oh no, Young-bok!

63
00:09:54,927 --> 00:10:01,392
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

64
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:09,609
I'm getting you in focus,
so try not to move.

65
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:16,240
This should work.

66
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:19,785
Okay, here we go.

67
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,455
Give me a smile.

68
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:24,999
Good.

69
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,418
One, two, three.

70
00:10:38,095 --> 00:10:39,013
What's the matter?

71
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:42,683
No, it's nothing.

72
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:46,604
I'm not sure I got the focus right.

73
00:10:47,980 --> 00:10:48,856
Excuse me.

74
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:50,900
Would you mind helping me?

75
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:51,984
Sorry?

76
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:57,198
I forgot my glasses today,
so I can't tell if the picture is blurry.

77
00:10:57,281 --> 00:10:58,616
I need your help.

78
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:02,161
I'll adjust the distance.

79
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:03,579
Just tell me when it looks clear.

80
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:05,790
Sure, I can do that.

81
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:08,376
Thank you. Here you go.

82
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:13,339
Let's make this quick. I'm starving.

83
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:17,426
I'll adjust it,
so tell me when it looks clear to you.

84
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,430
Give me a big smile.

85
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,314
Okay.

86
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:33,359
Is it clear?

87
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:36,821
I'm not sure.

88
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:38,030
Let's try again.

89
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,449
Give me a smile.

90
00:11:46,747 --> 00:11:48,332
Are you still not sure?

91
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:53,796
<i>Seolleongtang </i>delivery!

92
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:55,673
Hold on a second.

93
00:11:58,342 --> 00:11:59,760
What took you so long?

94
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:02,596
I've been having
tons of delivery orders today.

95
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:04,098
Ma'am, can I get some water?

96
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:06,392
Sure, water's in the room back there.

97
00:12:06,475 --> 00:12:08,060
- Can I get two glasses?
- Sure.

98
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:10,521
- What are you--
- One moment.

99
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:19,363
Must be crazy about each other.

100
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:26,662
What are you doing?

101
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:29,415
Just a moment.

102
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:40,885
Come on, let's go.

103
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:44,388
Okay, I'm coming!

104
00:12:47,808 --> 00:12:48,684
Still at it?

105
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,061
- Thanks for the water, ma'am.
- Sure.

106
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,688
I'll come back for the bowls tomorrow.

107
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:55,483
Thank you. See you.

108
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,609
Bye.

109
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,153
What took you so long?

110
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:02,072
Sorry, I had to grab some water.

111
00:13:02,156 --> 00:13:03,199
Let's go home.

112
00:13:04,074 --> 00:13:05,785
No-ma, I want candy.

113
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:10,414
Candy.

114
00:13:12,583 --> 00:13:13,959
Candy!

115
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:14,919
All right.

116
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,051
What was that all about?

117
00:13:25,638 --> 00:13:26,764
Did you cry?

118
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:31,227
No, I just…

119
00:13:31,894 --> 00:13:33,854
got something in my eye.

120
00:13:46,408 --> 00:13:48,160
Who was that just now?

121
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:49,829
A debt collector?

122
00:13:50,454 --> 00:13:51,288
Or…

123
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,457
your former lover?

124
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,626
What?

125
00:13:56,877 --> 00:13:58,170
A former lover?

126
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:00,381
If not, why would you hide?

127
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:03,092
What, were you afraid

128
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:07,179
of running into him after cheating on him?

129
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:09,765
Cheating?

130
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:14,603
What do you take me for?

131
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:20,651
Excuse me.

132
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:25,072
Oh boy.

133
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:29,368
I'm sorry.

134
00:14:32,371 --> 00:14:33,289
Ms. Keum.

135
00:14:36,375 --> 00:14:37,418
Ms. Keum!

136
00:14:48,387 --> 00:14:50,431
- How much is the candy?
- One jeon.

137
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,106
I'll take this one.

138
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:00,733
Thank you.

139
00:15:03,068 --> 00:15:05,404
- Sir, please buy some candy.
- Here.

140
00:15:08,616 --> 00:15:09,742
What's wrong?

141
00:15:10,701 --> 00:15:13,412
I just saw someone
who looked like Ga-kyung.

142
00:15:16,415 --> 00:15:17,750
I told you, Kkot-nim.

143
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,835
She's gone to America. Forget about her.

144
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:20,920
You won't see her again.

145
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:24,340
But I still miss her.

146
00:15:27,426 --> 00:15:28,385
Won't you eat your candy?

147
00:15:29,261 --> 00:15:30,888
I will.

148
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:31,889
Go on then.

149
00:16:05,798 --> 00:16:06,799
Back off.

150
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:17,226
Okay.

151
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:29,279
Hold on.

152
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:48,298
Move it over there.

153
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:14,950
SUSPECT'S DESCRIPTION
NAME: HAN CHEOL-YONG

154
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:18,370
Look over here.

155
00:17:19,329 --> 00:17:20,164
Not him.

156
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:24,209
Over that way!

157
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:26,378
Spread out and search!

158
00:17:41,935 --> 00:17:44,188
Please let me go.
My sister is waiting for me.

159
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:45,439
Will you shut up?

160
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:53,280
He's much older than me.

161
00:17:53,363 --> 00:17:54,531
Shut up.

162
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,369
Kkot-nim is waiting for me.

163
00:18:07,836 --> 00:18:08,837
FOR KIDS' CONSTIPATION

164
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:12,716
Sorry. I'm so sorry.

165
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:26,980
Were you trying to pick this up?

166
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:31,777
Is this yours?

167
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,820
Here.

168
00:18:32,903 --> 00:18:34,404
Why are you here alone?

169
00:18:35,823 --> 00:18:36,949
Don't you have any family?

170
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:39,785
I do have a family.

171
00:18:41,620 --> 00:18:43,288
I have an older sister

172
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:46,125
and an older brother.

173
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:51,130
My brother went to deliver <i>seolleongtang,</i>
so I'm waiting for him.

174
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:55,425
He said he'd be late if he took me along.

175
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:57,886
So he promised he'd be quick.

176
00:19:00,472 --> 00:19:03,142
I've waited and waited,

177
00:19:04,059 --> 00:19:05,978
but he hasn't come back.

178
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:18,365
I'm sorry I took so long.

179
00:19:19,408 --> 00:19:22,161
There are still police all over Jongno.

180
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:26,081
What about Sato?

181
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,000
Listen, Seok-jung.

182
00:19:28,792 --> 00:19:31,503
Forget about Sato for now.
Take care of yourself first.

183
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:34,548
You almost ended up six feet under
before he did.

184
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:38,468
In any case,
we need to get you to a hospital.

185
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:43,140
The trouble is,
there are wanted posters at the hospital.

186
00:19:44,016 --> 00:19:46,393
Apparently, the Gugukdan targeted Sato

187
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:48,395
in Dongsung-dong tonight but failed.

188
00:19:50,439 --> 00:19:52,608
Still, word is the Japanese police
took heavy losses.

189
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:55,986
The Gugukdan lost several members as well.

190
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:06,997
Over there!

191
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:20,052
My brother can run super fast.

192
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:23,513
He used to pull a rickshaw.

193
00:20:23,597 --> 00:20:26,099
But these days, he delivers <i>seolleongtang</i>

194
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:28,560
because he has a bicycle now.

195
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:32,606
He couldn't ride a bike before,

196
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:35,150
but now he rides well.

197
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:40,197
He says he can deliver
four bowls of <i>seolleongtang </i>at once.

198
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,782
Wow, that's amazing.

199
00:20:42,366 --> 00:20:44,701
- Right? Isn't he cool?
- He sure is.

200
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:46,328
Mak-dung.

201
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:48,080
- Mak-dung. Hurry, come eat.
- Okay.

202
00:20:48,163 --> 00:20:51,875
My brother brought me <i>seolleongtang</i>
the other day.

203
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:53,502
It was really good.

204
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:55,379
- Dad!
- Dad!

205
00:20:57,339 --> 00:21:01,343
He says I'll get a stomachache
if I eat too much <i>seolleongtang,</i>

206
00:21:01,426 --> 00:21:03,553
so I can only have it once a month.

207
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:05,389
That's a lie.

208
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:08,308
He's a terrible liar.

209
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,687
My sister says
it's because he has a good heart.

210
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,190
We're here. That's our house.

211
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:43,510
Aren't you hungry?

212
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:57,482
Wow, that looks yummy!

213
00:22:00,527 --> 00:22:01,695
Careful, it's hot.

214
00:22:01,778 --> 00:22:02,863
I'll cool it down for you.

215
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:14,791
Once you finish the porridge,
take your cold medicine.

216
00:22:14,875 --> 00:22:17,002
Kkot-nim! Bang Kkot-nim!

217
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,171
Bang Kkot-nim! Bang Kkot…

218
00:22:19,254 --> 00:22:20,297
Kkot-nim!

219
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:22,549
- Where were you?
- No-ma!

220
00:22:23,216 --> 00:22:24,301
Kkot-nim.

221
00:22:26,803 --> 00:22:29,222
How did you get home?
And what are you eating?

222
00:22:29,306 --> 00:22:30,849
And who are you?

223
00:22:37,564 --> 00:22:39,441
I'm home.

224
00:22:48,408 --> 00:22:49,409
Is no one home?

225
00:23:02,881 --> 00:23:03,965
What?

226
00:23:04,049 --> 00:23:05,342
A former lover?

227
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:07,969
Cheating?

228
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:10,222
Unbelievable.

229
00:23:10,305 --> 00:23:13,892
A rich kid's mind
really is a world of luxury.

230
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:18,063
I couldn't even afford to beat the cold,
let alone cheat on anybody.

231
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:24,945
Oh dear.

232
00:23:26,113 --> 00:23:27,406
Kkot-nim.

233
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:32,619
Why are you coughing? It breaks my heart.

234
00:23:48,885 --> 00:23:49,845
I suppose

235
00:23:50,762 --> 00:23:52,639
this is where it ends.

236
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:56,184
- Take him away.
- Yes, sir!

237
00:24:05,652 --> 00:24:08,029
Your plan worked brilliantly, sir.

238
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,575
The Gugukdan really did turn up.

239
00:24:11,658 --> 00:24:14,161
The one behind the attack
at Yoo Philip's house

240
00:24:14,244 --> 00:24:15,745
must be a member of the Gugukdan.

241
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:20,667
Do you realize how many officers we lost
just to kill one guy?

242
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:23,670
Did you even count them?

243
00:24:26,673 --> 00:24:27,507
I'm sorry, sir.

244
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:29,342
Hunt down every last one of them.

245
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:31,595
Wipe out the Gugukdan for good.

246
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:35,765
Get that guy first and round them all up.

247
00:24:39,394 --> 00:24:40,896
On it, sir!

248
00:24:43,815 --> 00:24:45,108
Inspector General!

249
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:46,735
Chief!

250
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:49,070
We caught him.

251
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:20,477
Hands in the air.

252
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:24,314
It's me.

253
00:25:41,414 --> 00:25:42,249
Are you hurt?

254
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:44,793
Han Cheol-yong…

255
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:47,379
is dead.

256
00:25:49,130 --> 00:25:51,258
The police have his body, so…

257
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:54,803
in case the police come searching,

258
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:58,139
I came to clear out his room.

259
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:04,437
Is this everything?

260
00:26:05,146 --> 00:26:06,189
Yes.

261
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:08,316
I think he cleaned it out beforehand.

262
00:26:09,067 --> 00:26:10,443
Let's get out of here then.

263
00:26:28,128 --> 00:26:30,005
<i>No nation in the world</i>

264
00:26:30,964 --> 00:26:34,217
<i>has the right to occupy</i>
<i>another country by force</i>

265
00:26:34,884 --> 00:26:38,513
<i>and oppress its people.</i>

266
00:26:41,308 --> 00:26:45,270
<i>The independence of our country</i>
<i>is only right,</i>

267
00:26:45,979 --> 00:26:47,564
<i>and it will inevitably come to pass.</i>

268
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:56,906
Oh no, Jeong-yeop.

269
00:26:59,242 --> 00:27:00,744
Jeong-yeop.

270
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,750
What in the world happened?

271
00:27:09,794 --> 00:27:11,338
Jeong-yeop!

272
00:27:11,421 --> 00:27:13,298
<i>If my death could bring about</i>

273
00:27:13,882 --> 00:27:17,344
<i>the independence of my nation</i>
<i>even a single second sooner,</i>

274
00:27:20,263 --> 00:27:24,017
<i>I hold no regrets at all.</i>

275
00:27:25,727 --> 00:27:26,811
<i>A man of Joseon.</i>

276
00:27:27,937 --> 00:27:30,649
<i>Han Cheol-yong.</i>

277
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:07,227
Madam.

278
00:28:18,613 --> 00:28:19,656
Madam.

279
00:28:28,957 --> 00:28:30,250
I'm coming in.

280
00:28:40,009 --> 00:28:41,720
Didn't she come home last night?

281
00:28:57,944 --> 00:28:59,279
Present arms!

282
00:29:07,704 --> 00:29:08,872
Welcome, sir.

283
00:29:10,039 --> 00:29:13,376
We didn't know you were returning
to Keijo today, Your Excellency.

284
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:15,044
How was your journey?

285
00:29:15,587 --> 00:29:18,131
About as peaceful as Keijo.

286
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:22,343
With scoundrels like Lee Bong-chang
and Lee Deok-ju around,

287
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:25,638
I have to hide my itinerary
and move around under the radar.

288
00:29:26,723 --> 00:29:28,933
You'd think I were some kind of criminal.

289
00:29:30,685 --> 00:29:34,314
So I hear there was a shootout
near Keijo Imperial University yesterday.

290
00:29:34,397 --> 00:29:35,440
Did you catch the culprit?

291
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:38,109
We shot one dead at the scene--

292
00:29:38,193 --> 00:29:39,360
Ever since you took office,

293
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:41,362
it seems those subversives

294
00:29:41,446 --> 00:29:44,824
have been running rampant,
don't you think?

295
00:30:12,435 --> 00:30:14,145
You can't die, Young-bok.

296
00:30:16,231 --> 00:30:18,316
You'd better not die, or you're fired.

297
00:30:24,197 --> 00:30:25,281
Who's there?

298
00:30:25,365 --> 00:30:27,700
Didn't I tell you to stay away
from my room?

299
00:30:27,784 --> 00:30:28,993
Miss.

300
00:30:29,077 --> 00:30:30,787
Your father is leaving now.

301
00:30:54,602 --> 00:30:55,562
Father.

302
00:30:56,145 --> 00:30:57,605
Have a good day.

303
00:30:57,689 --> 00:30:59,148
All right.

304
00:31:02,777 --> 00:31:04,696
Young-bok, that ungrateful brat.

305
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:06,573
I thought he was bright,

306
00:31:06,656 --> 00:31:08,658
so I sent him to school
and made him my butler.

307
00:31:08,741 --> 00:31:09,993
Yet over a little stomach bug,

308
00:31:10,076 --> 00:31:12,453
he wouldn't bother to show up
when I go to work?

309
00:31:13,997 --> 00:31:16,666
That's the problem
with these lowborn sorts.

310
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:17,959
I can't educate them.

311
00:31:18,042 --> 00:31:20,420
The king may say
the classes are all equal now.

312
00:31:20,503 --> 00:31:22,547
But generations of slave blood
run in his veins.

313
00:31:24,924 --> 00:31:28,052
Just because he piggybacked you
as a kid and grew up beside you,

314
00:31:28,136 --> 00:31:29,762
he forgot he's some lowborn nobody.

315
00:31:30,430 --> 00:31:31,431
For crying out loud.

316
00:31:33,641 --> 00:31:36,603
You hang around the Japanese
and think you're one of them now.

317
00:31:38,771 --> 00:31:39,772
What?

318
00:31:39,856 --> 00:31:41,274
What was that, Myung-nam?

319
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:43,985
It's nothing.

320
00:31:44,068 --> 00:31:47,614
I'll give Young-bok a proper earful,
so don't worry about it.

321
00:31:48,364 --> 00:31:50,742
Still, he's quite sick.
I'll let him take three days off.

322
00:31:50,825 --> 00:31:52,076
Fine.

323
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:54,996
But make sure those three days are unpaid.

324
00:31:55,622 --> 00:31:57,123
Sure, I'll handle it.

325
00:31:57,707 --> 00:31:59,125
Have a good day, Dad.

326
00:31:59,208 --> 00:32:00,168
You too.

327
00:32:13,389 --> 00:32:14,849
There you go.

328
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:17,143
Let's get this medicine down.

329
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:21,689
Down it goes.

330
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:23,900
All gone.

331
00:32:23,983 --> 00:32:25,068
Good job.

332
00:32:27,487 --> 00:32:29,572
So this was medicine for constipation?

333
00:32:29,656 --> 00:32:31,074
That's right.

334
00:32:31,574 --> 00:32:34,827
We don't know how to read,
so we had no idea what this was.

335
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:35,745
Right?

336
00:32:39,248 --> 00:32:42,919
That's why Ga-kyung drew this for us
before she left.

337
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:45,672
I miss her.

338
00:32:49,467 --> 00:32:50,426
Tell me about it.

339
00:32:53,304 --> 00:32:56,057
Ga-kyung, seriously…

340
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:57,976
- You know what?
- Yeah?

341
00:32:58,059 --> 00:33:03,773
I think the teacher
is the most handsome man I've ever seen.

342
00:33:03,856 --> 00:33:06,025
What? Who? That guy from yesterday?

343
00:33:06,109 --> 00:33:07,318
Yeah.

344
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:11,197
Hey, he's pale as a ghost,
like a walking tofu block.

345
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:12,657
You call that handsome?

346
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:14,909
And why are you calling him "teacher"?

347
00:33:14,993 --> 00:33:19,288
I asked him to teach me how to read,
so he's my teacher.

348
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:20,331
What?

349
00:33:21,708 --> 00:33:22,792
How to read?

350
00:33:22,875 --> 00:33:26,671
Yeah, he's going to come over
to teach me how to read.

351
00:33:26,754 --> 00:33:28,006
He promised me.

352
00:33:28,089 --> 00:33:30,800
Kkot-nim, you should've asked me first!

353
00:33:31,592 --> 00:33:34,262
I can't wait for him to come.

354
00:33:34,887 --> 00:33:37,974
Now I get to learn how to read
like Ga-kyung.

355
00:33:38,057 --> 00:33:39,267
I'm going to read!

356
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:41,102
Hey, Bang Kkot-nim!

357
00:33:44,814 --> 00:33:46,983
I just hope the boss doesn't catch us.

358
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:12,300
What? Did you have something to say?

359
00:34:12,967 --> 00:34:15,094
Things are tense
at the Government-General today.

360
00:34:15,178 --> 00:34:16,888
So don't wander around if you can.

361
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:19,766
You always tell me not to wander around.

362
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:22,602
Can I not even go to the bathroom?

363
00:34:23,728 --> 00:34:26,022
I'm saying,
don't wander around for no reason.

364
00:34:26,105 --> 00:34:28,107
I've never wandered around for no reason.

365
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:30,485
The only ladies' room
is in the corner on the first floor.

366
00:34:30,568 --> 00:34:31,944
So it just takes long.

367
00:34:32,028 --> 00:34:33,905
It's not like I'm slacking off.

368
00:34:34,614 --> 00:34:36,157
Very well, then.

369
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:38,493
Speaking of which,
I need to use the restroom.

370
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:41,329
You don't need to report that.

371
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:47,710
By the way…

372
00:34:50,546 --> 00:34:53,591
why are things tense around here?

373
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:01,307
Last night…

374
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:07,730
Yes, Sato speaking.

375
00:35:10,233 --> 00:35:12,110
Yes, it's almost done.

376
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:22,620
You complete idiot!

377
00:35:23,496 --> 00:35:25,623
What the hell were you thinking,
dropping this pipe?

378
00:35:27,333 --> 00:35:32,380
Even if you <i>Josenjings </i>work
your whole lives, you can't afford this!

379
00:35:32,463 --> 00:35:34,799
- Sorry, sir!
- I'm sorry!

380
00:35:34,882 --> 00:35:36,968
You'd better not put a scratch on it,

381
00:35:37,051 --> 00:35:39,846
or you'll pay with your lives!

382
00:35:41,347 --> 00:35:42,557
Do it properly!

383
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:44,016
I'm going to the bathroom.

384
00:35:46,602 --> 00:35:48,646
NO ENTRY

385
00:35:58,364 --> 00:36:00,575
I hope that damn murderer
drops dead in the street.

386
00:36:00,658 --> 00:36:02,785
All he ever says is "<i>Josenjing</i>."

387
00:36:03,369 --> 00:36:04,537
That wretched Japanese jerk.

388
00:36:04,620 --> 00:36:06,455
Hey, you okay after that beating?

389
00:36:06,539 --> 00:36:07,957
The same spot again, damn it.

390
00:36:14,714 --> 00:36:17,133
- Watch where you're going!
- I'm sorry.

391
00:36:33,983 --> 00:36:36,903
Well, well, look who it is.

392
00:36:38,321 --> 00:36:39,655
Your name was…

393
00:36:41,365 --> 00:36:42,783
Yes, I'm Keum Seo-hee.

394
00:36:43,367 --> 00:36:45,912
It's an honor that you recall me.

395
00:36:47,538 --> 00:36:48,664
Keum Seo-hee.

396
00:36:48,748 --> 00:36:50,249
Right.

397
00:36:50,333 --> 00:36:53,044
I did hear you joined us
as an interpreter trainee.

398
00:36:53,586 --> 00:36:57,006
I've been swamped
and couldn't make time to come say hi.

399
00:36:57,089 --> 00:36:58,799
Don't worry about it, sir.

400
00:36:58,883 --> 00:37:00,968
I should have been the one
to introduce myself.

401
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:03,930
Is Mr. Yoo doing well?

402
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:05,431
Yes, sir.

403
00:37:05,514 --> 00:37:09,060
If you have any trouble or need anything,
feel free to come see me.

404
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:11,354
Thank you very much.

405
00:37:13,105 --> 00:37:15,316
Joseon women are rather so boring.

406
00:37:16,984 --> 00:37:19,904
I suppose a woman educated by an American

407
00:37:21,405 --> 00:37:23,199
should be a bit different.

408
00:37:28,371 --> 00:37:29,580
Chief.

409
00:37:31,123 --> 00:37:32,333
Oh, Hideo.

410
00:37:33,751 --> 00:37:34,961
How have you been?

411
00:37:36,379 --> 00:37:37,546
Fine.

412
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:38,798
It's been a while.

413
00:37:40,758 --> 00:37:43,594
This is Keum Seo-hee,
an interpreter trainee.

414
00:37:43,678 --> 00:37:45,054
You've met her before, right?

415
00:37:47,056 --> 00:37:49,725
I'm sorry to interrupt your conversation,

416
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:52,311
but I was looking for Ms. Keum.
It's rather urgent.

417
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:57,233
Please take this up
to the Publications Division.

418
00:37:57,316 --> 00:37:58,317
It's on the fourth floor.

419
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:01,696
Yes, sir.

420
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:12,540
My apologies, Chief.

421
00:38:13,207 --> 00:38:14,959
It was an urgent matter.

422
00:38:17,044 --> 00:38:18,838
By the way, I heard there was a shootout

423
00:38:18,921 --> 00:38:21,173
with the Gugukdan
in Dongsung-dong last night.

424
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:25,886
I'm glad you weren't badly hurt.

425
00:38:28,597 --> 00:38:32,268
They came at us ready to die, yet
all they managed was this tiny scratch.

426
00:38:34,478 --> 00:38:36,939
How is it working with Ms. Keum?

427
00:38:37,023 --> 00:38:42,028
As you know, I was ordered to make sure
she was well taken care of.

428
00:38:43,446 --> 00:38:45,865
"Well taken care of," was it…

429
00:38:47,241 --> 00:38:49,785
Well, excuse me then.

430
00:38:56,292 --> 00:38:57,918
Two <i>Josenjings…</i>

431
00:38:59,295 --> 00:39:01,088
Well, isn't this interesting?

432
00:39:07,094 --> 00:39:08,095
Hideo.

433
00:39:10,514 --> 00:39:11,349
Yes?

434
00:39:17,646 --> 00:39:18,814
I'm back.

435
00:39:20,191 --> 00:39:22,818
I warned you not to wander around
for no reason.

436
00:39:24,945 --> 00:39:28,324
I wasn't. I was just coming back
from the bathroom.

437
00:39:29,950 --> 00:39:30,993
Last night…

438
00:39:33,621 --> 00:39:35,623
the Gugukdan tried to kill
the inspector general

439
00:39:35,706 --> 00:39:36,916
near Keijo Imperial University.

440
00:39:38,292 --> 00:39:41,212
After the shootout,
there were heavy casualties on both sides.

441
00:39:41,295 --> 00:39:43,506
We're hunting down
the remaining fugitives.

442
00:39:52,431 --> 00:39:55,017
That's why things are tense
around the office today.

443
00:39:59,438 --> 00:40:00,731
I see.

444
00:40:03,317 --> 00:40:04,151
Ms. Keum.

445
00:40:05,361 --> 00:40:06,195
Yes?

446
00:40:06,278 --> 00:40:08,447
You'll be working out of the office today.

447
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:10,533
It's an order from above.

448
00:40:11,909 --> 00:40:13,035
Out of the office?

449
00:40:55,828 --> 00:41:00,332
JONGNO POLICE STATION

450
00:41:25,065 --> 00:41:26,150
- Sir!
- Sir!

451
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:32,573
Maybe this fool inside
doesn't know Japanese.

452
00:41:32,656 --> 00:41:33,782
He hasn't said a word.

453
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:40,206
I was going to call
for a Joseon language interpreter.

454
00:41:41,749 --> 00:41:43,000
I'd appreciate your help.

455
00:41:43,834 --> 00:41:44,668
Sure.

456
00:41:45,586 --> 00:41:47,922
By the way…

457
00:41:49,298 --> 00:41:52,885
have you identified the fugitives
who got away yesterday?

458
00:41:54,887 --> 00:41:56,263
Why do you want to know?

459
00:41:57,348 --> 00:42:01,602
I thought it might be useful
while interpreting the interrogation.

460
00:42:01,685 --> 00:42:03,270
You don't need to know.

461
00:42:04,522 --> 00:42:05,356
Understood.

462
00:42:06,690 --> 00:42:08,984
Those bastards who ran took bullets.

463
00:42:09,902 --> 00:42:13,113
We're sweeping every hospital,
so they'll get caught soon enough.

464
00:42:14,490 --> 00:42:15,741
- Open the door.
- Yes, sir!

465
00:42:23,374 --> 00:42:24,375
Welcome, sir!

466
00:42:29,797 --> 00:42:30,673
Welcome.

467
00:42:32,132 --> 00:42:32,967
Come on in.

468
00:43:16,343 --> 00:43:20,431
Right after yesterday's shootout,
we spotted a suspicious guy in Jongno

469
00:43:20,514 --> 00:43:23,809
and combed the whole neighborhood.
Then we found him hiding.

470
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:26,061
Neither one has spoken yet,

471
00:43:26,145 --> 00:43:27,730
but he fits the description

472
00:43:27,813 --> 00:43:30,441
of the suspect who broke
into the American reporter's house.

473
00:43:31,692 --> 00:43:33,902
His old gunshot wound

474
00:43:34,820 --> 00:43:36,280
is badly infected,

475
00:43:36,822 --> 00:43:38,866
so he's burning up with a fever.

476
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:53,756
How are you?

477
00:43:54,715 --> 00:43:55,591
What's your name?

478
00:44:02,848 --> 00:44:03,682
Interpret that.

479
00:44:05,517 --> 00:44:06,477
Yes, sir.

480
00:44:08,187 --> 00:44:09,730
What is your name?

481
00:44:22,785 --> 00:44:24,870
If you won't talk on your own,

482
00:44:24,953 --> 00:44:26,830
I'll have no choice but to make you.

483
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:28,791
Go ahead.

484
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:01,115
Why are you out here?

485
00:45:01,198 --> 00:45:02,366
Jeez, you scared me.

486
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:05,494
I thought you were a ghost
from the crematorium.

487
00:45:05,577 --> 00:45:07,371
You almost gave me a heart attack.

488
00:45:08,455 --> 00:45:10,082
And stop talking nonsense.

489
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:14,461
That's a crematorium for the Jap.
Why would a Japanese ghost come here?

490
00:45:14,545 --> 00:45:17,339
It's all Gyodang-ri, either here or there.

491
00:45:17,423 --> 00:45:18,340
Yeah, right.

492
00:45:19,591 --> 00:45:20,801
Look at this.

493
00:45:20,884 --> 00:45:21,802
Right here.

494
00:45:22,469 --> 00:45:25,180
This is what the Japs did
just because we cried for independence.

495
00:45:25,264 --> 00:45:28,058
But they're all from the same Gyodang-ri?
Like hell.

496
00:45:30,811 --> 00:45:33,021
- What are you doing out here?
- What?

497
00:45:33,939 --> 00:45:35,441
Did something happen to Kkot-nim?

498
00:45:35,524 --> 00:45:36,734
No, not at all.

499
00:45:37,651 --> 00:45:40,696
I was just out watching the stars.

500
00:45:42,030 --> 00:45:44,533
You'll just get hungry if you stay up.
Go to sleep.

501
00:45:45,534 --> 00:45:47,244
Okay, good night.

502
00:45:49,079 --> 00:45:51,081
I thought the boss had caught us.

503
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:56,920
You pale tofu.
Don't you dare try something funny.

504
00:45:57,004 --> 00:45:58,046
<i>Giyeok.</i>

505
00:45:58,547 --> 00:45:59,381
<i>Giyeok.</i>

506
00:46:00,966 --> 00:46:02,092
<i>Giyeok.</i>

507
00:46:15,105 --> 00:46:17,649
Teacher, is something wrong?

508
00:46:17,733 --> 00:46:18,609
What?

509
00:46:19,193 --> 00:46:21,069
No, nothing's wrong.

510
00:46:21,153 --> 00:46:24,239
I don't believe you. You look so worried.

511
00:46:25,866 --> 00:46:26,784
Not at all.

512
00:46:27,826 --> 00:46:28,911
Are you done writing?

513
00:46:28,994 --> 00:46:30,621
- Let's see.
- Teacher.

514
00:46:30,704 --> 00:46:34,082
You should go.
I can see it all over your face.

515
00:46:34,833 --> 00:46:35,667
Go where?

516
00:46:40,255 --> 00:46:44,593
You've been wanting to go to the bathroom.
Am I right?

517
00:46:49,932 --> 00:46:53,894
The League of Nations Commission
will soon arrive in Keijo.

518
00:46:53,977 --> 00:46:57,731
To have the League of Nations recognize
Manchukuo's legitimacy,

519
00:46:58,232 --> 00:47:01,985
it is crucial that we show the Commission

520
00:47:02,069 --> 00:47:05,948
that Manchuria and Joseon are thriving
in peace and prosperity.

521
00:47:06,782 --> 00:47:07,616
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

522
00:47:08,784 --> 00:47:11,411
But in Manchuria,

523
00:47:11,954 --> 00:47:14,832
the Japanese army is being pushed around

524
00:47:14,915 --> 00:47:18,836
by rebels like Ji Cheong-cheon
and Yang Se-bong.

525
00:47:18,919 --> 00:47:21,672
And Kim Gu's stooges

526
00:47:21,755 --> 00:47:26,385
are sneaking into Joseon to kill me.

527
00:47:27,427 --> 00:47:29,096
Until the Commission arrives,

528
00:47:29,179 --> 00:47:32,724
the Government-General's top priority

529
00:47:32,808 --> 00:47:35,018
is to maintain public order in Keijo.

530
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:35,978
Is that clear?

531
00:47:36,061 --> 00:47:37,437
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

532
00:47:37,521 --> 00:47:38,647
Inspector General.

533
00:47:40,232 --> 00:47:41,400
You should see to it

534
00:47:41,483 --> 00:47:46,405
that the foreign press in Keijo
is handled with extreme care.

535
00:47:46,989 --> 00:47:50,909
Japan's deployment of the Kwantung Army
to Manchuria

536
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:55,330
was a legitimate act of retaliation

537
00:47:55,414 --> 00:47:59,084
against China's interference
with Japanese economic activity.

538
00:47:59,167 --> 00:48:00,544
Make that clear to the press.

539
00:48:01,503 --> 00:48:02,337
Understood.

540
00:48:03,714 --> 00:48:04,673
You may go.

541
00:48:09,595 --> 00:48:10,429
Yes, sir.

542
00:48:23,483 --> 00:48:24,359
Commander.

543
00:48:24,443 --> 00:48:25,319
Yes, sir.

544
00:48:25,986 --> 00:48:30,407
Do you think he fully understood
what I just said?

545
00:48:30,490 --> 00:48:31,533
Your Excellency.

546
00:48:32,117 --> 00:48:35,078
The Japanese in Joseon
are colonial residents.

547
00:48:35,162 --> 00:48:36,788
They aren't mainlanders like us.

548
00:48:37,372 --> 00:48:40,626
Colonial residents
are an inferior, lowborn lot.

549
00:48:41,126 --> 00:48:44,087
Men like him can scrub all they want,

550
00:48:44,171 --> 00:48:47,341
but they can't get the filth out
from under their nails.

551
00:48:47,424 --> 00:48:50,469
You should be especially wary of them.

552
00:48:51,595 --> 00:48:52,554
Very well.

553
00:48:53,055 --> 00:48:54,222
That's right.

554
00:49:01,438 --> 00:49:04,274
These <i>Josenjings </i>are like cockroaches.

555
00:49:04,358 --> 00:49:06,652
No matter how many we crush,
they keep crawling back.

556
00:49:07,235 --> 00:49:09,321
Is this your stubborn nature?

557
00:49:09,404 --> 00:49:12,866
Did you think we'd be impressed
and hand you your independence?

558
00:49:18,246 --> 00:49:19,289
What are you doing?

559
00:49:19,831 --> 00:49:20,832
Interpret that.

560
00:49:20,916 --> 00:49:21,792
Yes.

561
00:49:24,002 --> 00:49:24,920
He says

562
00:49:25,879 --> 00:49:28,924
that people of Joseon continue to fight
for independence.

563
00:49:31,176 --> 00:49:32,135
That's it?

564
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:34,012
Why was that so short?

565
00:49:35,555 --> 00:49:36,765
I'm sorry.

566
00:49:37,307 --> 00:49:39,434
I was trying to find
the right Joseon words

567
00:49:39,518 --> 00:49:40,602
to capture your meaning.

568
00:49:43,105 --> 00:49:46,733
He's asking if you think
this will ever lead to independence.

569
00:49:48,527 --> 00:49:51,321
There's something
I'm genuinely curious about.

570
00:49:51,405 --> 00:49:54,574
Do you, independence fighters,
the Gugukdan or whatever,

571
00:49:54,658 --> 00:49:57,035
honestly believe you can save Joseon?

572
00:49:57,661 --> 00:49:58,954
He's asking if you think

573
00:49:59,037 --> 00:50:01,707
the independence fighters can save Joseon.

574
00:50:03,667 --> 00:50:05,877
Don't you want to answer,
or don't you know?

575
00:50:07,212 --> 00:50:08,964
Then I'll tell you.

576
00:50:11,633 --> 00:50:12,801
You…

577
00:50:12,884 --> 00:50:15,762
Your so-called independence movement
is ruining Joseon.

578
00:50:16,722 --> 00:50:19,516
You're holding on to a dead hope

579
00:50:19,599 --> 00:50:22,185
and instigating the barbaric <i>Josenjings.</i>

580
00:50:22,686 --> 00:50:26,440
You traitors are robbing them
of the honor of being reborn

581
00:50:27,274 --> 00:50:29,609
as loyal subjects
of the Great Empire of Japan.

582
00:50:30,944 --> 00:50:33,613
Do you realize how pathetic it is

583
00:50:34,322 --> 00:50:36,616
to cling to a hope that's already dead?

584
00:50:42,581 --> 00:50:43,874
The independence fighters

585
00:50:44,583 --> 00:50:46,585
are ruining Joseon.

586
00:50:47,502 --> 00:50:49,713
You're holding on to a long-dead hope,

587
00:50:50,547 --> 00:50:51,715
instigating barbaric--

588
00:50:51,798 --> 00:50:53,467
Why is it taking you so long?

589
00:50:55,177 --> 00:50:56,887
You're instigating the barbaric <i>Josenj…</i>

590
00:50:56,970 --> 00:50:58,597
people of Joseon.

591
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:00,974
You're committing treason
by robbing them of the chance

592
00:51:01,058 --> 00:51:03,518
of being reborn as subjects
of the Great Empire of Japan.

593
00:51:15,322 --> 00:51:17,115
You pathetic <i>Josenjing.</i>

594
00:51:17,199 --> 00:51:21,203
I bet you felt like a hero
while plotting your grand scheme.

595
00:51:23,080 --> 00:51:24,581
But look at you now.

596
00:51:24,664 --> 00:51:25,832
Look around this room.

597
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:28,293
Who do you have around you?

598
00:51:29,836 --> 00:51:32,172
Did you promise to keep your mouth shut
if you got caught?

599
00:51:35,801 --> 00:51:37,177
Did you take an oath or something?

600
00:51:38,303 --> 00:51:42,224
Now you're learning the hard way

601
00:51:43,016 --> 00:51:46,770
how pointless an oath
made by lowborn scum like you actually is!

602
00:51:50,148 --> 00:51:51,399
Your grand scheme…

603
00:51:52,526 --> 00:51:53,610
Do you understand me?

604
00:51:55,278 --> 00:51:57,614
A miserable, meaningless death all alone.

605
00:51:58,490 --> 00:52:01,159
That's all the <i>Josenjing</i>
independence movement will ever achieve.

606
00:52:03,286 --> 00:52:05,205
I said, do you understand?

607
00:52:05,288 --> 00:52:08,166
You filthy <i>Josenjing </i>roaches.

608
00:52:11,920 --> 00:52:13,839
Why isn't he saying anything?

609
00:52:15,173 --> 00:52:17,551
Are you interpreting my words properly?

610
00:52:17,634 --> 00:52:19,511
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee.

611
00:52:23,014 --> 00:52:25,475
Interpreter trainee Keum Seo-hee!

612
00:52:35,235 --> 00:52:36,278
Who are you?

613
00:52:39,406 --> 00:52:40,657
You.

614
00:52:41,658 --> 00:52:43,160
You're that live-in maid, aren't you?

615
00:52:47,164 --> 00:52:49,291
Why are you using that name?

616
00:52:49,916 --> 00:52:50,750
Why?

617
00:52:54,087 --> 00:52:55,714
What is he talking about?

618
00:52:55,797 --> 00:52:57,048
What are you all doing?

619
00:52:57,132 --> 00:52:58,884
Is that your real name?

620
00:52:59,467 --> 00:53:01,094
Is that really your name?

621
00:53:01,761 --> 00:53:03,763
Who the hell are you?

622
00:53:07,434 --> 00:53:09,102
Answer me!

623
00:53:09,186 --> 00:53:11,813
Why are you using her name?

624
00:53:15,025 --> 00:53:16,860
What's this lunatic saying now?

625
00:53:16,943 --> 00:53:18,862
Who are you really?

626
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,740
I said, who are you?

627
00:53:21,823 --> 00:53:23,783
Interpret that, Keum Seo-hee!

628
00:53:38,924 --> 00:53:40,842
Why, Interpreter Sato.

629
00:53:41,509 --> 00:53:43,511
What brings you all the way here?

630
00:53:48,516 --> 00:53:49,434
By any chance,

631
00:53:49,935 --> 00:53:52,312
did you come by to check on Ms. Keum?

632
00:53:54,064 --> 00:53:56,733
I'm here to see
if the work is being handled properly.

633
00:53:59,194 --> 00:54:02,113
As you can see, she's--

634
00:54:02,197 --> 00:54:03,073
No.

635
00:54:04,699 --> 00:54:06,159
I'm talking about you, Chief.

636
00:54:07,661 --> 00:54:11,915
I'd like to hear what you've found out
from him so far.

637
00:54:12,832 --> 00:54:15,460
You pulled an English interpreter trainee

638
00:54:15,543 --> 00:54:19,714
from the Foreign Affairs Division
to interrogate in the Joseon language.

639
00:54:20,882 --> 00:54:24,344
I suppose you've found out
quite a lot by now.

640
00:54:27,138 --> 00:54:28,098
Well, then,

641
00:54:28,181 --> 00:54:29,724
tell me what you've found out.

642
00:54:30,308 --> 00:54:33,311
What was his motive
for targeting the inspector general?

643
00:54:33,395 --> 00:54:34,938
What is his name?

644
00:54:35,021 --> 00:54:37,107
What did you find out about the Gugukdan?

645
00:54:39,567 --> 00:54:41,319
You insolent <i>Josenjing!</i>

646
00:54:41,945 --> 00:54:45,699
How dare a mere interpreter
speak to me like that!

647
00:54:47,701 --> 00:54:49,286
I've spoiled you like a young master,

648
00:54:49,369 --> 00:54:51,955
and now you seem
to have forgotten your place.

649
00:54:52,038 --> 00:54:55,375
Do you really think
you're the inspector general's son?

650
00:54:56,084 --> 00:54:58,211
You're nothing but a <i>Josenj…</i>

651
00:55:08,847 --> 00:55:10,390
Inspector General.

652
00:55:20,358 --> 00:55:22,402
- When did you get here--
- Finish what you were saying.

653
00:55:26,323 --> 00:55:27,574
I'm intrigued.

654
00:55:28,658 --> 00:55:30,493
If Hideo isn't my real son,

655
00:55:33,621 --> 00:55:34,456
then what is he?

656
00:55:43,798 --> 00:55:44,966
Please forgive me!

657
00:55:45,467 --> 00:55:47,344
Please forgive my outburst, sir!

658
00:55:55,769 --> 00:55:56,895
I apologize for the trouble.

659
00:55:59,481 --> 00:56:01,232
Make sure she gets home safely.

660
00:56:01,316 --> 00:56:02,275
Interpreter Sato.

661
00:56:38,728 --> 00:56:41,022
Sir, please allow me to explain--

662
00:56:46,486 --> 00:56:47,612
Forgive me, sir!

663
00:56:47,695 --> 00:56:50,949
Did you forget Keum Seo-hee
is involved with that American reporter?

664
00:56:52,325 --> 00:56:53,660
Did you forget how critical

665
00:56:53,743 --> 00:56:57,247
foreign press coverage of Joseon is
because of Manchukuo?

666
00:56:59,332 --> 00:57:03,253
You learned nothing
from what happened in 1919.

667
00:57:06,756 --> 00:57:07,757
Did you forget

668
00:57:08,675 --> 00:57:10,927
how "that incident" blew up

669
00:57:11,010 --> 00:57:13,012
after the Americans reported it abroad?

670
00:57:14,055 --> 00:57:15,223
I am deeply sorry, sir.

671
00:57:19,018 --> 00:57:20,311
Utter idiot.

672
00:57:44,794 --> 00:57:45,712
Ms. Keum.

673
00:57:51,301 --> 00:57:52,218
My apologies.

674
00:57:54,220 --> 00:57:56,014
I assure you it won't happen again.

675
00:58:02,187 --> 00:58:03,104
That being said…

676
00:58:06,900 --> 00:58:08,026
I'd appreciate it…

677
00:58:10,945 --> 00:58:12,614
if today's incident didn't reach

678
00:58:14,532 --> 00:58:15,700
the foreign press.

679
00:58:19,954 --> 00:58:21,456
I mean, Mr. Yoo.

680
00:58:52,529 --> 00:58:54,113
Have you found out who he is?

681
00:58:54,197 --> 00:58:55,949
Not yet, sir. My apologies.

682
00:58:57,492 --> 00:58:58,618
But he keeps insisting

683
00:58:59,118 --> 00:59:02,747
that he and that man
are not members of the Gugukdan.

684
00:59:04,249 --> 00:59:05,542
We'll find out soon.

685
00:59:05,625 --> 00:59:08,211
I'd prefer if they were the Gugukdan.

686
00:59:11,798 --> 00:59:14,551
Did you know your fellow members
were killed in Dongsung-dong?

687
00:59:21,099 --> 00:59:22,725
We've identified him, sir.

688
00:59:22,809 --> 00:59:23,893
Is that so?

689
00:59:23,977 --> 00:59:26,020
Yes, we found him in the watchlist files.

690
00:59:26,104 --> 00:59:27,438
His name is Na Byeong-sun.

691
00:59:27,522 --> 00:59:29,566
He lives in Anseong-gun,
Gyeonggi Province.

692
00:59:30,650 --> 00:59:31,484
See?

693
00:59:32,068 --> 00:59:33,695
You can hold your tongue all you want,

694
00:59:33,778 --> 00:59:35,655
but we find everything out eventually.

695
00:59:36,239 --> 00:59:38,491
What's the point of wasting time
like this?

696
00:59:39,784 --> 00:59:41,744
Bring his wife and children here. Now.

697
00:59:41,828 --> 00:59:42,704
Yes, sir.

698
00:59:46,374 --> 00:59:48,960
Let's see if he'll stay quiet
once we put his family

699
00:59:49,043 --> 00:59:50,420
hanging in front of him.

700
00:59:58,177 --> 01:00:00,263
You'd better start talking.

701
01:00:00,346 --> 01:00:01,764
Unless you want to watch

702
01:00:01,848 --> 01:00:04,350
your family die in front of you.

703
01:00:06,853 --> 01:00:08,271
My family?

704
01:00:29,417 --> 01:00:30,710
Shut up!

705
01:00:47,727 --> 01:00:50,063
So it won't leak to foreign outlets?

706
01:00:50,813 --> 01:00:51,856
Yes.

707
01:00:53,900 --> 01:00:55,068
If news of this

708
01:00:56,861 --> 01:00:58,488
gets out overseas,

709
01:00:59,822 --> 01:01:00,948
it could be a problem…

710
01:01:05,161 --> 01:01:07,288
Mr. Yoo is a journalist, after all.

711
01:01:10,291 --> 01:01:11,501
I'd appreciate your discretion.

712
01:01:19,217 --> 01:01:20,635
Understood.

713
01:01:22,887 --> 01:01:25,515
Thank you for kindly reminding me
how I became

714
01:01:25,598 --> 01:01:28,226
an interpreter trainee
at the Government-General.

715
01:01:32,397 --> 01:01:33,773
Thank you for everything.

716
01:01:35,149 --> 01:01:37,026
- Ms. Keum.
- I'll go by myself.

717
01:02:43,509 --> 01:02:45,511
What, are you going somewhere?

718
01:02:45,595 --> 01:02:48,222
I'm done playing spy. Goodbye.

719
01:02:48,306 --> 01:02:49,766
You're quitting?

720
01:02:49,849 --> 01:02:50,850
Yes!

721
01:02:50,933 --> 01:02:52,435
I quit.

722
01:02:52,518 --> 01:02:55,396
I shouldn't have gotten involved
in this mess in the first place.

723
01:02:55,897 --> 01:02:57,774
I don't want to die for nothing.

724
01:02:59,066 --> 01:03:00,026
"Die for nothing"?

725
01:03:00,109 --> 01:03:02,153
Right, for nothing.

726
01:03:02,862 --> 01:03:05,531
Look, you went
to Dongsung-dong yesterday, didn't you?

727
01:03:06,407 --> 01:03:07,492
When I found out,

728
01:03:07,575 --> 01:03:10,286
I wondered if you'd been dead or arrested.

729
01:03:10,369 --> 01:03:13,372
I went to Jongno Police Station today
worried sick about you.

730
01:03:13,456 --> 01:03:16,584
I could barely catch my breath
until I realized it wasn't you.

731
01:03:17,543 --> 01:03:20,797
But do you know
what I had to do there today?

732
01:03:22,632 --> 01:03:26,177
I interpreted the interrogation
of a captured independence fighter.

733
01:03:29,138 --> 01:03:31,140
"You damn <i>Josenjing."</i>

734
01:03:31,682 --> 01:03:34,769
"I bet you felt like a hero
while plotting your grand scheme."

735
01:03:34,852 --> 01:03:37,063
"But look at you now.
Who do you have around you?"

736
01:03:37,146 --> 01:03:39,232
"You'll die for nothing all alone."

737
01:03:39,315 --> 01:03:42,151
"That's all the <i>Josenjing</i>
independence movement will ever achieve."

738
01:03:42,235 --> 01:03:44,737
"You filthy <i>Josenjing </i>roaches!"

739
01:03:46,364 --> 01:03:47,907
I spent the whole day

740
01:03:48,908 --> 01:03:50,952
having to translate those insults.

741
01:03:51,619 --> 01:03:54,330
The man they'd arrested
wouldn't say a single word.

742
01:03:54,413 --> 01:03:56,499
I was the only one talking back and forth

743
01:03:56,582 --> 01:03:58,668
between the chief of police and that man.

744
01:04:00,002 --> 01:04:01,879
I didn't know
you'd be put in that position.

745
01:04:01,963 --> 01:04:02,922
But did you think

746
01:04:04,048 --> 01:04:06,050
being a spy was all fun and games?

747
01:04:09,387 --> 01:04:12,098
You said you didn't care
about the independence movement.

748
01:04:12,181 --> 01:04:14,809
Then why take it so hard
that you interpreted those words

749
01:04:14,892 --> 01:04:16,269
for an independence fighter?

750
01:04:17,895 --> 01:04:19,480
Who says I'm taking it hard?

751
01:04:19,564 --> 01:04:20,731
I'm not.

752
01:04:20,815 --> 01:04:23,526
It's just that once my cover gets blown,

753
01:04:23,609 --> 01:04:26,362
I'll end up arrested like him
and killed for nothing.

754
01:04:26,445 --> 01:04:30,491
I refuse to die a meaningless death.
So I'm out right here and now.

755
01:04:30,575 --> 01:04:31,826
Watch your mouth!

756
01:04:32,827 --> 01:04:34,078
"A meaningless death"?

757
01:04:35,913 --> 01:04:38,416
How can you say that
about someone who was captured

758
01:04:38,499 --> 01:04:40,459
fighting for our nation's independence?

759
01:04:44,547 --> 01:04:47,592
No Joseon person would ever
call that sacrifice meaningless.

760
01:04:47,675 --> 01:04:49,302
In fact, anywhere in the world,

761
01:04:49,385 --> 01:04:51,470
dying for your country's freedom

762
01:04:51,554 --> 01:04:53,472
is never considered a meaningless death.

763
01:04:54,056 --> 01:04:55,558
Don't kid yourself.

764
01:04:56,475 --> 01:04:58,519
I'm no independence fighter.

765
01:04:59,020 --> 01:05:00,021
You see,

766
01:05:00,104 --> 01:05:03,524
I took the job at the Government-General
since you promised to send me to America.

767
01:05:03,608 --> 01:05:05,985
But if my cover gets blown,

768
01:05:06,068 --> 01:05:09,155
I'll look like an independence fighter
in their eyes.

769
01:05:09,238 --> 01:05:11,991
How am I different from the man
they interrogated today?

770
01:05:12,074 --> 01:05:15,661
I was posing as an interpreter trainee,
and he was posing as a deliveryman.

771
01:05:15,745 --> 01:05:16,871
That's the only difference.

772
01:05:16,954 --> 01:05:18,205
It's the same thing!

773
01:05:19,749 --> 01:05:20,583
A deliveryman?

774
01:05:20,666 --> 01:05:21,542
Yes.

775
01:05:21,626 --> 01:05:22,752
It was him.

776
01:05:22,835 --> 01:05:25,296
The one who got into this house
posing as a deliveryman.

777
01:05:26,964 --> 01:05:29,425
No matter how well you cover your tracks--

778
01:05:29,508 --> 01:05:30,468
You mean…

779
01:05:32,219 --> 01:05:34,347
he was the one who came here to kill Sato?

780
01:05:34,430 --> 01:05:35,598
Right.

781
01:05:36,140 --> 01:05:37,767
On the night of the dinner,

782
01:05:37,850 --> 01:05:39,477
he came into this house with a gun

783
01:05:39,560 --> 01:05:41,687
disguised as a deliveryman from Itsukoshi.

784
01:05:41,771 --> 01:05:43,564
He's not part of the Gugukdan, is he?

785
01:05:43,648 --> 01:05:44,523
Did he…

786
01:05:47,026 --> 01:05:48,736
say something?

787
01:05:50,863 --> 01:05:52,531
What did he say?

788
01:05:52,615 --> 01:05:53,699
Say?

789
01:05:54,241 --> 01:05:55,993
I wish he had said a single word.

790
01:05:56,077 --> 01:05:57,244
He wasn't cooperative at all.

791
01:05:57,328 --> 01:05:58,829
So the interrogation took all day.

792
01:05:59,705 --> 01:06:02,500
It was like
he was set on keeping his mouth shut.

793
01:06:02,583 --> 01:06:04,126
That is, until he heard my name.

794
01:06:04,210 --> 01:06:07,171
All of a sudden,
he started asking who I was.

795
01:06:07,254 --> 01:06:10,675
He went wild and yelled about
why I was using that name.

796
01:06:14,053 --> 01:06:14,929
Your name?

797
01:06:17,056 --> 01:06:18,099
Lee Ga-kyung?

798
01:06:18,808 --> 01:06:19,642
What?

799
01:06:20,768 --> 01:06:21,644
No.

800
01:06:22,144 --> 01:06:23,562
Keum Seo-hee, obviously.

801
01:06:30,444 --> 01:06:32,405
The moment he heard that name, he started…

802
01:06:42,123 --> 01:06:42,957
What's going on?

803
01:06:54,802 --> 01:06:56,012
<i>Seo-hee</i>

804
01:06:56,721 --> 01:06:58,222
was my daughter's name.

805
01:07:00,766 --> 01:07:03,310
My daughter, the one killed
by the inspector general.

806
01:07:08,524 --> 01:07:09,442
Don't tell me…

807
01:07:11,318 --> 01:07:12,194
Is he…

808
01:07:16,323 --> 01:07:18,576
your husband?

809
01:07:23,664 --> 01:07:25,958
Your daughter, Keum Seo-hee.

810
01:07:27,668 --> 01:07:30,004
Is he the father of your daughter?

811
01:07:31,672 --> 01:07:32,506
Is he?

812
01:07:35,760 --> 01:07:36,719
Is he really?

813
01:07:38,012 --> 01:07:39,847
Is that true? Really?

814
01:07:58,616 --> 01:08:00,701
You people are insane!

815
01:08:01,285 --> 01:08:03,370
Is independence really worth all this?

816
01:08:03,454 --> 01:08:05,915
You're here like this, and your husband…

817
01:08:05,998 --> 01:08:09,043
He's lying there covered in blood,
beaten half to death.

818
01:08:12,671 --> 01:08:15,257
I'm not dying
getting caught up in this madness.

819
01:08:15,925 --> 01:08:18,260
I'm out. I'm calling it quits.

820
01:08:18,344 --> 01:08:21,138
I told you. There's no mercy for traitors.

821
01:08:21,222 --> 01:08:22,681
Go right ahead.

822
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:25,684
You made me a spy,
but you never trusted me.

823
01:08:25,768 --> 01:08:28,062
What kind of spy is that?
And what did I betray?

824
01:08:28,145 --> 01:08:30,022
- Lee Ga-kyung.
- Get your hands off me!

825
01:08:38,280 --> 01:08:40,449
This is insane.

826
01:08:55,339 --> 01:08:56,173
Oh no.

827
01:08:58,259 --> 01:08:59,218
No.

828
01:09:25,411 --> 01:09:26,996
Why's everything such a mess?

829
01:09:55,399 --> 01:09:56,358
Keum Seo-hee.

830
01:10:13,250 --> 01:10:14,460
Who?

831
01:10:15,211 --> 01:10:17,046
I don't know anyone by that name.

832
01:11:11,934 --> 01:11:18,565
A MAN OF JOSEON
HAN CHEOL-YONG

833
01:11:18,649 --> 01:11:22,569
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

834
01:11:22,653 --> 01:11:23,821
<i>Keum Seo-hee.</i>

835
01:11:24,780 --> 01:11:26,740
<i>She's going to rely on you a lot.</i>

836
01:11:28,117 --> 01:11:28,993
INTERPRETER SATO HIDEO

837
01:11:29,076 --> 01:11:29,994
<i>Seo-hee's father.</i>

838
01:11:30,077 --> 01:11:31,453
What are you planning to do?

839
01:11:31,537 --> 01:11:33,205
<i>What Sato wants to hide the most…</i>

840
01:11:33,998 --> 01:11:35,666
A mass murderer.

841
01:11:35,749 --> 01:11:38,544
If Sato realizes he was one of the victims
from the Kyeam-ri massacre,

842
01:11:38,627 --> 01:11:41,338
<i>there's a chance he'll find out who I am.</i>

843
01:11:43,173 --> 01:11:44,341
Keum Seo-hee.

844
01:11:44,425 --> 01:11:46,427
<i>Win Sato Hideo's heart.</i>

845
01:11:46,510 --> 01:11:47,761
Get him on your side.

846
01:11:48,721 --> 01:11:51,515
Should I end things with Mr. Yoo?

847
01:11:51,598 --> 01:11:53,350
She needs to trust you, but…

848
01:11:53,434 --> 01:11:54,268
<i>Ms. Keum!</i>

849
01:11:54,351 --> 01:11:56,478
<i>Never let yourself have personal feelings.</i>

850
01:12:03,944 --> 01:12:05,946
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
